00:00:52.580 --> 00:01:00.860
That being said, my question is, there's a
really big gap between scientists and the

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:09.409
general public, and it feels like the gap
keeps growing and it gets more and more difficult

00:01:09.409 --> 00:01:18.509
to convey to the general public the precise
nature of science and the difficulties associated

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:19.509
with it.

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:26.270
And it feels like scientists are failing as
a political entity to talk to the general

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.270
public.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.270
How do you feel about this?

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.270
Speaker 1: I agree with you.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.689
I mean, I think here's the thing.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:37.869
If you told me I'm not a scientist, but I
my instinct is if you told scientists you

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:42.450
are failing as a political entity, they would
say we're not a political entity.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:48.919
And I but at the same time, I acknowledge
what you're saying, which is we I mean, maybe

00:01:48.919 --> 00:01:53.489
it's science education that's failing and
critical thinking and epistemology.

00:01:53.489 --> 00:01:54.989
I don't I don't know.

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:56.210
But you're absolutely right.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.809
In your in your observation about the effects
of it.

00:01:59.809 --> 00:02:02.229
Speaker 4: What can we do?

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:11.230
Because I have I spent so much time thinking
about this because in light of global warming.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.600
It's way worse than what most reports suggest.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:23.360
The most people don't know this, but the IPCC
is meant to be a sort of a politically favorable

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.360
take on that.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:29.519
It doesn't take into account multiple feedback
loops, including the tying of the permafrost

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:30.519
in the Arctic.

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:35.879
It doesn't take into account ocean salinity,
which changes the CO2 dissolved in the oceans

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:38.690
exactly like multiple feedback loops going
on.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:45.870
All of which suggest that the reality of climate
change is going to be way worse than what

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:46.870
most people expect.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:47.870
Hmm.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.090
Speaker 1: The situation is more dire.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.430
In other words.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.760
Speaker 4: Yes.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.760
Yes.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:58.939
The IPCC reports are the best case scenario,
the best possible hypothetical scenario.

00:02:58.939 --> 00:03:04.900
And it's and yet so many scientists I know
personally and I've talked to them about this,

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.069
they are they struggle to get people to understand
this.

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:15.370
And they're worried that if they actually
talk about what's going to happen with real

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:20.340
precision and actual facts, that they'll be
dismissed as apocalyptic loons.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.340
Right.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:25.499
Speaker 1: So and they probably go they're
probably correct to think that that's what

00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:26.499
would happen.

00:03:26.499 --> 00:03:27.499
Yeah.

00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:28.499
I don't know how to bridge the gap, Rose.

00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:34.439
I mean, this is this is an ongoing conversation
where it almost feels too late for so many

00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:35.439
people.

00:03:35.439 --> 00:03:40.989
And there's also the political machine that
that wants to stay on fossil fuels that we're

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:42.170
up against.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:45.830
And we need to start teaching critical thinking
and media literacy very early.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:52.159
I actually have a bunch of books waiting to
be read on a pilot that deal directly with

00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:53.159
this issue.

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:57.269
And so I'm hoping in a few months maybe I'll
have some greater insights into it, but you're

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.340
at least identifying the problem correctly.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.629
